  "notes": "{皆|みな} means \"everyone\" or \"all.\" It functions as both a noun and adverb.\n\nFORMALITY LEVELS:\n- {皆|みな}: standard/formal\n- みんな: casual (more common in speech)\n- {皆|みな}さん: everyone (polite address)\n- {皆|みな}{様|さま}: everyone (very formal/business)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {皆|みな}で: together, all together\n- {皆|みな}が: everyone (as subject)\n- {皆|みな}に: to everyone\n- {皆|みな}の: everyone's\n\nAS ADVERB (ALL):\n- お{金|かね}は{皆|みな}{使|つか}った: spent all the money\n- {料理|りょうり}は{皆|みな}{食|た}べた: ate all the food\n\nEXAMPLES:\n- {皆|みな}さん、おはようございます: Good morning, everyone\n- {皆|みな}で{行|い}こう: Let's all go together",
